    "answer_text": "The environment is defined as the totality of man’s surroundings - both natural and man-made. Environmental Pollution is injection of harmful substances into the environment. It is result of industrialisation. Pollution changes the physical, chemical and biological characteristics of air, land and water. Pollution harms human life and the life of other species. It also degrades living conditions while wasting or depleting raw material resources.",
